# A claim written before a purge and re-creation of the leaf is raised after it.
# The retirement reset the leaf's entry, so a raise checked against the entry
# alone accepts an epoch the old incarnation already superseded, and its activation
# appends. The shard does not check the retired floor on appends (#5635), so the
# raise's floor check is the only guard.
MODULE: StaleEpochNeverAppendsIgnoresRetiredFloor
TARGET: StaleEpochNeverAppends
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the claim's raise is not refused at or below the retired floor
PERTURBS: ClaimRaise
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] >= Max2(fence, memFence)
    /\ epoch[a] > retired
--- REPLACE
    /\ epoch[a] >= Max2(fence, memFence)
\* MUTATION: the retired floor is not checked at the raise.
--- END